		On one hand, noting that $$4\log r-2\log (\epsilon+r_\epsilon^2)=O(\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{\delta})$$ and
		\begin{align*}
			\left|\nabla_g\left(4\log r-2\log (\epsilon+r_\epsilon^2)\right)\right|^2&= \left|D\left(4\log r-2\log (\epsilon+r_\epsilon^2)\right)\right|^2+(g^{-2}-r^{-2})\left|\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\left(-2\log (\epsilon+r_\epsilon^2)\right)\right|^2\\
			&=O(\frac{\epsilon}{\delta^2})=o(\sqrt{\epsilon}),
